{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class Text_Document_Analysis {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        br.readLine();\n        String input = br.readLine();\n        \n        int maxWordLength = Arrays.stream(input.split(\"\\\\([a-zA-Z_]*\\\\)\"))\n            .flatMap(part -> Arrays.stream(part.split(\"_+\")))\n            .mapToInt(String::length)\n            .max()\n            .orElse(0);\n        \n        int identifierCount = 0;\n        boolean inParens = false;\n        boolean prevWasLetter = false;\n        \n        for (char c : input.toCharArray()) {\n            if (c == '(') {\n                inParens = true;\n                prevWasLetter = false;\n            } else if (c == ')') {\n                inParens = false;\n                prevWasLetter = false;\n            } else if (inParens && Character.isLetter(c)) {\n                if (!prevWasLetter) {\n                    identifierCount++;\n                }\n                prevWasLetter = true;\n            } else {\n                prevWasLetter = false;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(maxWordLength + \" \" + identifierCount);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cctype>\n\nint main() {\n    std::string line;\n    std::getline(std::cin, line); // Skip first line\n    std::getline(std::cin, line);\n    \n    std::string input = line;\n    \n    // Split by pattern \\([a-zA-Z_]*\\) and find max word length\n    std::vector<std::string> parts;\n    size_t i = 0;\n    while (i < input.length()) {\n        if (input[i] == '(') {\n            // Skip until closing parenthesis\n            while (i < input.length() && input[i] != ')') {\n                i++;\n            }\n            if (i < input.length()) i++; // Skip the closing ')'\n        } else {\n            size_t start = i;\n            while (i < input.length() && input[i] != '(') {\n                i++;\n            }\n            if (i > start) {\n                parts.push_back(input.substr(start, i - start));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    int maxWordLength = 0;\n    for (const auto& part : parts) {\n        size_t start = 0;\n        for (size_t j = 0; j <= part.length(); j++) {\n            if (j == part.length() || part[j] == '_') {\n                if (j > start) {\n                    maxWordLength = std::max(maxWordLength, static_cast<int>(j - start));\n                }\n                start = j + 1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // Count identifiers inside parentheses\n    int identifierCount = 0;\n    bool inParens = false;\n    bool prevWasLetter = false;\n    \n    for (char c : input) {\n        if (c == '(') {\n            inParens = true;\n            prevWasLetter = false;\n        } 